,"videoTitle":"Country music legend Dolly Parton dies at the age of 80","program":"- The Hill News Video","fullEpisode":true,"framerate":"24","airDate":"1787682240","videoDuration":"96","originalVideoTitle":"Country music legend Dolly Parton dies at the age of 80"},"12103411":{"videoId":"12103411","videoTitle":"Trump: Navy cleared mines in Strait of Hormuz, new mines will be 'systematically destroyed'","program":"- The Hill News Video","fullEpisode":true,"framerate":"24","airDate":"1787680200","videoDuration":"164","originalVideoTitle":"Trump: Navy cleared mines in Strait of Hormuz, new mines will be 'systematically destroyed'"},"12103365":{"videoId":"12103365","videoTitle":"Mike Lindell accuses MN Secretary of State of unlawful recount process","program":"- The Hill News Video","fullEpisode":true,"framerate":"60","airDate":"1787679300","videoDuration":"174","originalVideoTitle":"Mike Lindell accuses MN Secretary of State of unlawful recount process"},"12102408":{"videoId":"12102408","videoTitle":"DC Bureau: Trade War Escalates","program":"-- FAST Only","fullEpisode":true,"framerate":"30","airDate":"1787663820","videoDuration":"73","originalVideoTitle":"DC Bureau: Trade War Escalates"},"12100815":{"videoId":"12100815","videoTitle":"BREAKING: Supreme Court backs Trump's order to limit mail-in ballots ahead of midterms | NEWSNATION","program":"- The Hill News Video","fullEpisode":true,"framerate":"24","airDate":"1787611800","videoDuration":"148","originalVideoTitle":"BREAKING: Supreme Court backs Trump's order to limit mail-in ballots ahead of midterms | NEWSNATION"},"12103448":{"videoId":"12103448","videoTitle":"Battleground Republicans seek distance from Trump on key issues | THE FIGHT FOR 2028","program":"- The Hill News Video","fullEpisode":true,"framerate":"24","airDate":"1787681160","videoDuration":"155","originalVideoTitle":"Battleground Republicans seek distance from Trump on key issues | THE FIGHT FOR 2028"}},"poster":"https:\/\/h104216-ucdn.mp.lura.live\/iupl_lin\/D76\/226\/D76226D4A887515A98ADBD4FEC428E2C.jpg?aktaexp=2082787200&aktasgn=540385f406b24c6650960d0eb98978a8","sources":[{"src":"https:\/\/tkx.mp.lura.live\/rest\/v2\/mcp\/video\/12106712.m3u8?anvack=Rawk5AaXamlYMHRoV0UeKfkdB3KQ0dnD&eud=NExlctJX0MT7X8mwrM3XdzqUHVjPM0Frsq9TRUEb4ak%2FKJgRKZ%2B64LxwkKEbw%2B0YTyO8KsbFw40vgX8hrw%2Bxqw%3D%3D","videoType":"video","renderMethod":"static"}],"title":"Hakeem Jeffries dismisses Kushner meeting concerns: Lindsey Granger | RISING","error":null,"playerId":"nxsplayer_b550782b9a","adTagUrl":"https:\/\/pubads.g.doubleclick.net\/gampad\/ads?sz=1x1000&iu=\/5678\/nx.thehill\/opinion\/opinions___lindsey_s_lens&ciu_szs=300x250&impl=s&gdfp_req=1&env=vp&output=vmap&unviewed_position_start=1&ad_rule=1&description_url=https:\/\/thehill.com\/opinion\/lindseys-lens\/6052835-jeffries-kushner-private-meeting\/&vconp=2&cust_params=station%3DTheHill%26pid%3D6052835%26pers_cid%3Dthehill-2-article-6052835%26vidcat%3D\/opinion\/opinions___lindsey_s_lens%26bob_ck%3D[bob_ck_val]%26d_code%3D1%26pagetype%3Dstory%26hlmeta%3D6052835%20jeffries%20kushner%20private%20meeting%26aa%3Df&vid=12106712&cmsid=2594591"}"> NOW PLAYING Hakeem Jeffries met privately with Jared Kushner,&nbsp;and everybody has questions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

The New York Times reported Sunday that the House Democratic&nbsp;leader&nbsp; had a private meeting with President&nbsp;Trump&rsquo;s son-in-law to discuss potential areas of common ground.&nbsp;&nbsp;

On the surface, that&rsquo;s politics. Jeffries could soon be Speaker if Democrats win the House, so having conversations with people close to the White House makes sense. Probably would make more sense to people who actually have jobs&nbsp;in&nbsp;the White House,&nbsp;but I digress.&nbsp;

Jeffries&nbsp;then&nbsp; posted this video &nbsp;defending the meeting.&nbsp;

&ldquo;He asked for a meeting and I took it,&nbsp;to discuss the affordability crisis that exists that is not a hoax. At the&nbsp;same period in&nbsp;time &mdash;&nbsp;I shouldn&rsquo;t have to say&nbsp;it,&nbsp;but I am&nbsp;&mdash; no one is going to get a pass.&nbsp;We&rsquo;re&nbsp;gonna&nbsp;hold every single member of the&nbsp;Trump&nbsp;cartel accountable, beginning on day one,&rdquo; said the House minority leader.&nbsp;&nbsp;

OK. But I have&nbsp;questions.&nbsp;First, why are you dressed like&nbsp;it&rsquo;s&nbsp;St. Patrick&rsquo;s Day?&nbsp;&nbsp;

Jeffries says&nbsp;in&nbsp;that moment he just finished community work, and&nbsp;maybe that&rsquo;s&nbsp;exactly what happened. But the video felt very intentional and like trying too hard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Back to Hakeem Jeffries meeting with Jared Kushner. Trump has called Jeffries a &ldquo;thug&rdquo; and attacked his intelligence as&nbsp;low&nbsp;IQ, and Jeffries has spent years portraying Trump as extreme and corrupt, vowing to hold him accountable.&nbsp;So&nbsp;meeting with Kushner about affordability doesn&rsquo;t exactly make sense.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Jeffries has longstanding ties to the pro-Israel political and donor network. Campaign-finance tracking shows&nbsp;roughly $1.7 million&nbsp;in AIPAC-linked support over his political career, depending on how broader affiliated spending is counted.&nbsp;Of course&nbsp;that does not prove AIPAC had anything to do with this meeting,&nbsp;but it is relevant context:&nbsp;Kushner also has longstanding financial and diplomatic connections involving Israel, including large donations to AIPAC.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Take a look&nbsp;at&nbsp; this New York Times headline : &ldquo;Kushner&rsquo;s Financial Ties to Israel Deepen Even With&nbsp;Mideast Diplomatic Role&rdquo;&nbsp;&nbsp;

The Times previously reported that while Kushner was serving in the first&nbsp;Trump&nbsp;administration, his family real estate company received&nbsp;roughly $30 million&nbsp;from one of the largest Israeli insurers. His company also took loans from Bank Hapoalim, Israel&rsquo;s largest bank.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Again,&nbsp;none of that tells us what was discussed between Kushner and Jeffries, but it tells us this&nbsp;isn&rsquo;t&nbsp;simply two guys talking about the price of eggs.&nbsp;There are significant political, diplomatic and financial relationships surrounding both men,&nbsp;and that&rsquo;s why people are asking questions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Tommy Vietor&nbsp; put it bluntly :&nbsp;&ldquo;Jared Kushner has no actual government job he just uses his family connections to get money from gulf autocrats and fund corrupt deals. The only way @RepJeffries should work with him is with demands for documents and subpoenas.&rdquo;&nbsp;&nbsp;

Kushner has no formal government job right now, yet he has extraordinary access to the president and Jeffries could soon have extraordinary power in Congress.&nbsp;&nbsp;

So&nbsp;maybe this&nbsp;meeting&nbsp;really was&nbsp;about affordability.&nbsp;Maybe it&nbsp;was simply a potential Speaker talking to someone who has the president&rsquo;s ear. But if&nbsp;that&rsquo;s&nbsp;the case, Democrats deserve more transparency&nbsp;&mdash; so&nbsp;why was it a secret?&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

Jeffries cannot spend years promising to hold the Trump administration accountable and then expect people not to question private meetings with one of Trump&rsquo;s closest family members.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Lindsey Granger is a NewsNation contributor and co-host of The Hill&rsquo;s commentary show &ldquo;Rising.&rdquo; This column is an edited transcription of her on-air commentary.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;

